# Example path-scoped rule for Claude Code.
# This rule fires whenever the agent reads or writes a file matching the
# patterns below, regardless of which folder the agent is working from.
#
# Path-scoped rules complement nested AGENTS.md files. Nested AGENTS.md applies
# when the agent works *inside* a folder; path-scoped rules apply whenever a
# *file pattern* is touched. Use path-scoped rules when:
#   - The rule must fire regardless of cwd (e.g., "all files in research/ must
#     cite primary sources" should fire even when the agent is working from root)
#   - The rule applies to file types rather than directories (e.g., "all .sql
#     files must use parameterized queries")
#
# Adjust the `paths` list and the rule body to match this project's actual
# conventions, then commit. Delete this file if you don't need path-scoped
# rules.
paths:
  - "**/*.md"
